===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tyme}}, {{m|enm|time}}, from {{inh|en|ang|tīma|t=time, period, space of time, season, lifetime, fixed time, favourable time, opportunity}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*tīmō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*tīmô|t=time}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*deh₂imō}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*deh₂y-|t=to divide}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|tym}}, {{m|sco|tyme||time}}, {{cog|gsw|Zimen}}, {{m|gsw|Zimmän|Zīmmän|time, time of the year, opportune time, opportunity}}, {{cog|da|time||hour, lesson}}, {{cog|sv|timme||hour}}, {{cog|no|time||lesson, hour}}, {{cog|fo|tími||hour, lesson, time}}, {{cog|is|tími||time, season}}. Related to {{m|en|tide}}. Not related to {{noncog|la|tempus}}.

